    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **James Wood** (76.28) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) headline our lineup as the premier plays. **James Wood** benefits from a massive matchup grade against a vulnerable 8.31 xERA arm, providing the ceiling we crave in a high-efficiency offensive environment. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** leverages a massive 14% park factor boost and an advantageous platoon split against Leiter, making him an elite option to anchor our production. While **Tyler Soderstrom** (71.17) rounds out our trio of top-tier starts, he thrives primarily on the SP_xERA volatility of Kochanowicz, offering significant upside against a suspect pitching profile.\n\nThe bench decision process was disciplined, with **Austin Riley** (54.52) narrowly edging out other utility options despite his unfavorable 7th-spot order placement. While **Kyle Karros** (51.98) offers a favorable park boost, the optimizer favored **Austin Riley**\u2019s base projection, viewing his matchup against Junk as slightly more stable. We remain in a holding pattern regarding our high-impact injured reserve contingent, specifically **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, **Trevor Story**, and **Giancarlo Stanton**, as their absence continues to compress our bench flexibility. We are closely monitoring the status of prospects like **Carson Williams**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Henry Bolte** to ensure our depth remains capable of covering for current mainstays like **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, and **Gabriel Moreno**.\n\nRisk management remains a primary focus today. We are tracking a marginal disadvantage for **Zach McKinstry** (47.79) due to a negative platoon split against Bibee, pushing his efficiency score dangerously close to our \"Below Floor\" threshold. While we are starting him to avoid wasting limited game caps, he is the first candidate to be subbed if defensive replacements or late-inning pivots are required. Owners should verify final lineups, as any negative weather shifts or last-minute defensive adjustments could necessitate a pivot from our lower-scoring marginal starts, ensuring we maintain our aggressive pursuit of the SB category without sacrificing excessive efficiency points.",
